From 9b51e6ea22adbb5bf6f92be1d124944b9a5f8f13 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 21:55:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(engine): leave an EXCEPT of a key a lazy function's
 domain lacks to TLC's warning

TLC reads a function at an EXCEPT's key before it updates it
(FcnLambdaValue.select): where a function it keeps lazy has an
earlier EXCEPT at the key or its domain holds it, the EXCEPT is kept;
elsewhere the function is left as it is and TLC warns that the EXCEPT
was applied to non-existing fields (2144). The engine left the
function as it is without the warning, and the trace evaluator failed
as at an application outside the domain. Both now treat the key as
they treat a key any other function lacks: the engine leaves it to
the reference interpreter, and the evaluator declines where TLC warns
and keeps the function under -nowarning. 5 runs of the upstream
conformance suite that printed no warning now decline.
